  "rules": [
    {
      "id": "u1",
      "text": "A reviewer never wrote code in the slice it reviews."
    },
    {
      "id": "u2",
      "text": "No cross-vendor reviewer unless the owner asks."
    },
    {
      "id": "u3",
      "text": "Roles on the orchestrator's own agent run as subagents; a role on another agent runs headless in the slice worktree with the same brief."
    },
    {
      "id": "u4",
      "text": "\"well specified\" means the slice names its files, failing tests, implementation steps and checks, and needs no open owner decision."
    },
    {
      "id": "u5",
      "text": "Split a slice only into parts with disjoint files and their own tests; a slice too big for one implementer is two slices or a slivered slice."
    },
    {
      "id": "u6",
      "text": "Sliver a slice only at effort 1, or at effort 2 when every sliver is effort 1; never at effort 3."
    },
    {
      "id": "u7",
      "text": "Slivers with disjoint files and their own tests may run in parallel, at most 3 at once; the rest run in order."
    },
    {
      "id": "u8",
      "text": "A sliver that fails its gate twice, or whose diff falls short of the orchestrator's check, moves to the next model up (haiku to sonnet high)."
    },
    {
      "id": "u9",
      "text": "The orchestrator reads a Haiku implementer's diff itself before review, and switches that role to Sonnet early when quality falls short."
    },
    {
      "id": "u10",
      "text": "A slice that touches the UI (internal/tui and its golden views, docs/dashboard.md, internal/cli output, or a ui.* adj key) also runs the UI pass row (r14) as its own role, in parallel with the reviewer, not instead of it, on every size. The UI pass runs as a general-purpose subagent (it needs the Skill tool), loads the tui-design:tui-design and frontend-design:frontend-design skills (plugins enabled in .claude/settings.json), edits nothing, and sends suggested design edits to the orchestrator for the implementer; the gate still decides. Folding it into the relay-reviewer on size S was tried and dropped on 2026-10-26 (owner): relay-reviewer has no Skill tool. A vendor that cannot load these skills gets ork's vendor-neutral UI prompt instead. This holds for each slice in a wave."
    },
    {
      "id": "u11",
      "text": "The spec check before a wave runs the Spec check row (r16): one read-only pass over every ticked slice, answered in one sitting. It is a reviewer row only until slicer has a spec-check role (s392); it is never a fallback of the reviewer or the gate, and the reviewer's rule u1 does not apply to it because it reads specs and writes no code."
    }
  ],
  "next_row": 17,
